WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
Spring 1912.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:07.290
At the head of the dinner table, a wealthy
manufacturer makes a confident speech.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.700
There will be no war, he says.

4
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.220
And the new ship, the
Titanic, can never sink.

5
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:17.310
But the first audience,
in 1945, knew better.

6
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.480
The Titanic sank in April 1912.

7
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.080
Two world wars followed.

8
00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.470
By the end of the night, the
parents have heard everything.

9
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.990
So why do they learn nothing?

10
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.000
In this mission, you'll see
how the audience's hindsight,

11
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.280
called dramatic irony, turns
his confidence against him.

12
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.710
You'll meet Sybil Birling, and
the charity committee she chairs.

13
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.290
And you'll watch both parents in
Act 3, once the Inspector has gone.

14
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.880
Your mission: explain why
the parents learn nothing.
